          "source": "docs/validation/shimmer_ab_v2/diagnostics/diagnostic_window_footprint_average_always.json",
          "hypothesis": "Diagnostic, not a fix: the shipped footprint average only fades in where a floor spans under about 31 pixels, so a near facade is still drawn from one sample per pixel. Forcing the average on everywhere supersamples the window light sixteen times at every distance. If the remaining shimmer is point sampling of the window pattern \u2014 pane edges above all, since the blinds and curtains were measured to carry little \u2014 this removes most of it; if it does not, the cause is not in the window light's sampling.",
